      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "There is no measure currently available to identify asthmatics with potential immune incompetence."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "We propose use of a novel scoring system called the FACT score, which is formulated based on four parameters: (1) Family history of asthma, (2) Atopic conditions, (3) Bacterial colonization and (4) Th1 versus Th2 immune profile."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "This was a cross-sectional study involving 16 asthmatics and 14 non-asthmatics. The first two parameters of the FACT score were obtained via a chart review and interview. For the third parameter, nasopharyngeal swab samples were cultured. The ratio of interleukin-5 to interferon-gamma for each patient was measured by peripheral blood mononuclear cells cultured with house dust mite. Antibodies to 23 pneumococcal antigens were used for humoral immunity."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The FACT scores for asthmatics (mean\u2009±\u2009SD: 5.2\u2009±\u20091.87) were higher than those for non-asthmatics (mean\u2009±\u2009SD: 3.3\u2009±\u20091.5) (p\u2009=\u20090.008). Of the 16 asthmatics, 7 (44%) had 12 or more positive serotype-specific polysaccharide antibodies, whereas 12 of 14 (86%) of non-asthmatics subjects had 12 or more positive serotype-specific polysaccharide antibodies (p\u2009=\u20090.014). Overall, the FACT score was inversely correlated with the number of positive serotype-specific antibody levels [rho (ρ)\u2009=\u2009-0.38, p\u2009=\u20090.04]. The proportions of subjects with 12 or more positive serotype-specific antibodies among non-asthmatics and asthmatics below and above the median of the FACT scores were 86, 50 and 38%, respectively (p\u2009=\u20090.052)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "The FACT score may help us identify a subset of asthmatics with immune incompetence. Study findings need to be replicated in a larger study."
        }
      ]},
